content:
A post about how I’ve noticed that many people still think you need specialist knowledge for VibeCoding – that’s not the case 🧐

----------------------------------

▪️ Rent a VPS server on Contabo or somewhere else;
▪️ Install Visual Studio Code and use it to connect Claude Code to your server;
▪️ Type into the standard Claude chat what you want to do, in your own words;
▪️ It draws up a plan and provides prompts for Claude Code for each point – you simply paste them into the VS Code chat;
▪️ Get on with your own things and watch the results; 

---------------------------------- 

Essentially, you discuss the plan with one Claude, get the prompts, paste them into the chat of the other one, and that’s it.

By the way, you can also get detailed instructions from Claude for each of the points.  

We’re living in a time of enormous possibilities – surely you must have some ideas about what to build?

